# Keeps the build context small for infra/deploy/*/Dockerfile, which COPY the
# whole repo into the pruner stage (see those Dockerfiles' comments). None of
# this is needed to compute a turbo prune graph or to run apps/api / apps/worker.
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.turbo
.git
.superpowers
.claude
.vscode
*.tsbuildinfo

# Python islands — never touched by the Bun images.
apps/ml/.venv
apps/ml/cache
apps/ml/**/__pycache__
research/.venv
research/**/__pycache__

# Mobile/native build output — not part of any workspace apps/api or
# apps/worker depends on, but excluded explicitly since it's large.
apps/mobile/.expo
apps/mobile/ios
apps/mobile/android

# Terraform. `.terraform/` is the extracted AWS provider — ~650MB, i.e. it was
# by far the largest thing in this context and the reason `turbo prune` looked
# slow (the COPY . . before it, not the prune). The state files matter for a
# second reason: Terraform writes SSM SecureString values to state in
# PLAINTEXT, so tfstate/tfvars carry the Redis password, Supabase keys and
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY. Nothing here is needed to build a Bun image.
# The whole directory, rather than globs per file type: a Bun image needs
# nothing from it, and one directory line can't be defeated by the fact that
# `*.tfstate` in a .dockerignore only matches at the context ROOT (same reason
# node_modules is listed twice above).
infra/deploy/terraform

# Defense in depth, for Terraform state that ever lands outside that directory.
**/.terraform
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.*
**/*.tfvars

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
